:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:5.6.25</span></span>For small <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_p^\\perp Hp$\">$v\\in T_p^\\perp Hp$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H_{\\exp _p(v)}=\\{ h\\in H_p\\mid Dh|_pv=v\\} $\">$H_{\\exp _p(v)}=\\{ h\\in H_p\\mid Dh|_pv=v\\} $</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23cor%3Apet-ch5-isotropy-near-orbit\">↗ cor:pet-ch5-isotropy-near-orbit</a> \\sketch By <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_GeodesicsAndDistance%23thm%3Apet-ch5-slice-theorem\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-slice-theorem\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-74686d3a7065742d6368352d736c6963652d7468656f72656d\">subsection 6.4</a>, equivariant slice coordinates are unique. Thus <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h$\">$h$</span> fixes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p(v)$\">$\\exp _p(v)$</span> exactly when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h\\in H_p$\">$h\\in H_p$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Dh|_p(v)=v$\">$Dh|_p(v)=v$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-slice-theorem","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#cor:pet-ch5-conjugate-isotropy-manifold","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_GeodesicsAndDistance#thm:pet-ch5-slice-theorem","title":"thm:pet-ch5-slice-theorem